# Ruling 31 (2026-07-26) - FORENSIC RUNTIME LOGS ARE NOT SOURCE.
# These are append-only records of what AUREA actually did at runtime. They are
# machine-written, environment-specific, and a committed copy is guaranteed to
# be a merge conflict and a false-pressure vector: a test run's entries in a
# forensic log are records of nothing she survived.
#
# BOTH FILES WERE TRACKED until this ruling, which is why the previously
# deferred .gitignore line would have been INERT - git keeps updating a tracked
# file no matter what is ignored. They were untracked with `git rm --cached`,
# which destroys nothing: every committed version stays in git history
# permanently, and history is never amended here.
#
# Both writers mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True), so a fresh clone recreates
# them on first use. Verified.
logs/*.jsonl
data/collapse_logs/*.jsonl
